<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-8 mt-40" id="faq">
<div class="text-center mb-16">
<span class="inline-block px-4 py-1 rounded-full bg-tertiary-fixed/50 text-on-tertiary-fixed-variant font-semibold text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-6">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="font-headline text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-on-surface tracking-tighter">Questions we get every week.</h2>
</div>
<div class="space-y-4">

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">How much does junk removal cost?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
We price by load size. Minimum load starts at $125. A quarter load is $175, half is $350, three-quarter is $525, and a full 12x8x5 dump trailer is $699. Labor, dump fees, and taxes are already in those numbers. See the full <a href="/pricing.html" class="text-primary font-semibold underline decoration-primary/30">pricing page</a> for details.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">How soon can you come out?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
Most jobs run within 2 to 3 days. Same-day and rush jobs are possible and carry a percentage premium. Text us the job and we'll quote the rush number up front, no surprise.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">Do you do demolition too?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
Yes. Sheds, decks, fences, hot tubs, interior walls, and concrete slab breakout on smaller jobs. We do the teardown and the haul-away in one visit. For structural demolition (a full house or anything load-bearing at scale), we'll tell you up front if it's beyond our scope.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">Are there items you won't take?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
We can't take hazardous materials in large quantities: paint, solvents, chemicals, propane tanks, pesticides, or pressure-treated wood in bulk. One old paint can in a garage cleanout is fine. A stack of fifteen is a hazmat job, and San Diego County has a free drop-off we'll point you to.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">What areas do you serve?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
Poway, San Diego, Escondido, Oceanside, San Marcos, Ramona, Rancho Bernardo, Carlsbad, Vista, and most of North County. If you're further out, send a text anyway. For bigger demolition jobs we'll drive past the usual radius.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">What if the pile is bigger than the photo?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
It happens about 15 to 30% of the time. Before we load anything past the original tier, we tell you the new number. If you want to stop or skip items at that point, no pressure.
</div>
</details>

<details class="group bg-surface-container-lowest rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 ring-1 ring-outline-variant/20">
<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none">
<h3 class="font-headline text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-on-surface pr-4">Are you licensed and insured?</h3>
<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">add</span>
</summary>
<div class="mt-4 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
Yes. credential details available with full general liability insurance and workers' comp on every job. Happy to send the paperwork to your HOA or property manager if they ask.
</div>
</details>

